      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability: removing unused imports, extracting intermediate results to named variables, and adding meaningful comments/assertion messages.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed all unused imports (`StringWriter`, `Objects`, `Builder`, `StrBuilder`, `TextStringBuilder`, `ParameterizedTest`, `ValueSource`), extracted `join(...)` call results into named variables (`resultAfterVarargs`, `resultAfterIterable`) instead of nesting them inside `assertEquals`, replaced cryptic `// does not throw IOException` comments with explanations of *why*, and added assertion messages to make test failures self-describing."
